  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Protection and Humanitarian Assistance to Vulnerable Venezuelans in Border Areas in Venezuela and Brazil</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian needs persist in Venezuela, despite a limited improvement in macroeconomic indicators. Lack of sufficient fuel availability remains a priority issue, affecting all sectors of the economy, including food production and transportation. The loss of revenue has significantly limited investment in public services and continues to impact the supply of electricity, water, domestic gas and telecommunications and has also severely affected the health sector. The intervention aims to provide protection and humanitarian assistance to vulnerable Venezuelans in border areas in Venezuela and in the Northern region of Brazil, with a particular focus on people on the move. The action is implemented through a multisectoral integrated approach, with a focus on following priorities sectors: shelter and non-food items, food security, protection, and coordination.</narrative>
  </description>
